        "<b>Passage 1:</b><br><br>Every person is said to be either a risk-taker or risk-averse. A risk-taker have high tolerance on risks while a risk-averse person have low risk tolerance. That is, if two persons are to invest on an asset, a risk-taker would be willing to invest on a high risk asset while a risk-averse person would choose a low risk asset.<br><br>Generally, high risk assets give a higher yield of return than low risk assets. That is how the sellers of the assets entice investors to buy their products. Investors would not want to buy high risk assets with low yield, so suppliers allot a higher yield to offset the risk of the asset. Thus, a risk-taker would be able to expect to receive a higher yield than a risk-averse person.",
